title: Importer Overview
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

JSON Convert's difficulty is all in //authoring//: records paths,
ancestor scopes, transforms, normalization.  None of it is needed at
//use// time.  An importer separates the two.

* ''The author'' -- you, here in the Studio -- pastes a sample of the JSON, builds and tests a profile against it, and clicks ''Generate importer…''.  Out comes a plugin file.
* ''The recipient'' drags that file into their wiki.  A page appears, named for the data.  They paste their JSON, click ''Stage invoices'', look over the list, click ''Apply''.

The importer is a plugin in the ordinary TiddlyWiki sense: one tiddler
to install, one to delete, listed in the control panel with a readme.
It depends on the JSON Convert //runtime// plugin, which holds the
engine and the panel.  The generator can bundle the runtime into the
same file, so a wiki with nothing installed still needs only one drag.

What the recipient sees is the whole pitch:

[img[Import Page.png]]

Two importers in one wiki never collide: each keeps its working data
under its own name, and nothing it does reaches disk until ''Apply''.
